; -*- mode: lisp -*-
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The suite's own column, stated once: its listing line and where it came
; from. Both used to be literals in task.py's register_suite call; the loader
; that carried them is gone, and this file is what the registry reads instead.
;
; NOTHING ELSE IS SHARED, deliberately. Two variants, and each states its whole
; staging itself -- the cell, the arm and which hand works, the arrangement,
; the rig, the servo gains -- each beside the comment a reader wants next to
; it. That is not an oversight of a shared column: the two documents differ in
; almost every one of those keys, because one receptacle is bolted to a bench
; and the other is 90 g of metal the support hand carries into the air. A
; :staging block up here would be a list of things both documents override.
;
; The description carries parentheses and the provenance a semicolon, so both
; are quoted strings: inside "..." the reader takes ";" and "(" literally.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(define (suite usbc_insert)

  (:language "Mate a x2-scale USB-C plug into a receptacle that is either bolted down (port) or
              held in the air by the other hand (bulkhead) -- 0.15 mm-class fit, hydroelastic
              pair on the free one, YAM i2rt bimanual.")

  ; Headline first; every document beside this file, and only those.
  (:variants bulkhead port insert_easy insert_medium insert_easy_nocable insert_medium_nocable)

  ; The tier is each document's own (:provenance (:tier ...)), stated where its
  ; thresholds are -- `port` is a reproduction and `bulkhead` is original. What
  ; is here is the suite's origin, verbatim from the loader that used to carry
  ; it.
  (:provenance
    (:source "Ported from newton_tasks/sim/yam_usbc_mjc_sim.py (single-model MuJoCo variant) at
              defaults for port; bulkhead is authored over it and inherits its thresholds
              verbatim, the two mouths being coplanar on one mate line by construction. Meshes
              from newton_tasks Assets/usb_c_mesh plus Bulkhead.stl, unmodified. On bulkhead
              only, post-release retention is a modeled detent -- a criterion-gated weld standing
              in for the shield spring this contact stack cannot express
              (tasks/usbc_insert/assets/entity.py.SpecUsbcDetent records the evidence); a success
              claims seated-to-click-depth, and entry is untouched contact physics.")
  )
)
